1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:02,432
A doctor reads blood pressure.

2
00:00:02,432 --> 00:00:04,568
A tyre shop checks air pressure.

3
00:00:04,568 --> 00:00:06,501
A diver feels water pressure.

4
00:00:06,901 --> 00:00:08,709
Three pressures, three places.

5
00:00:08,709 --> 00:00:10,933
But what is pressure actually made of?

6
00:00:11,383 --> 00:00:15,321
Diya's pressure cooker whistles when
the steam pushes hard enough on the

7
00:00:15,321 --> 00:00:16,221
lid.

8
00:00:16,136 --> 00:00:19,965
Can we write that pressure using
only mass, length and time?

9
00:00:19,965 --> 00:00:21,530
No units, no numbers.

10
00:00:22,030 --> 00:00:25,500
By the end, you will build it
yourself, one block at a time.

11
00:00:26,150 --> 00:00:28,552
So what is a dimensional formula?

12
00:00:28,902 --> 00:00:33,146
It shows how a quantity depends on
mass, length and time, and with which

13
00:00:33,146 --> 00:00:34,046
powers.

14
00:00:34,143 --> 00:00:38,879
We write it inside square brackets,
as M to the a, L to the b, T to the

15
00:00:38,879 --> 00:00:39,779
c.

16
00:00:39,669 --> 00:00:44,699
Written as an equation, like velocity
equals LT to the minus one, it is

17
00:00:44,699 --> 00:00:46,372
a dimensional equation.

18
00:00:46,772 --> 00:00:48,191
The trick is simple.

19
00:00:48,191 --> 00:00:52,885
Start from a formula you know, and
replace every quantity by its dimensions.

20
00:00:53,535 --> 00:00:56,559
Let's watch the cooker lid
on our motion notebook.

21
00:00:56,909 --> 00:00:58,680
Steam pushes up on the lid.

22
00:00:58,680 --> 00:01:00,405
That push is a force, F.

23
00:01:00,405 --> 00:01:03,115
It is spread over the area of the lid, A.

24
00:01:03,515 --> 00:01:06,198
As the steam heats up, the force grows.

25
00:01:06,198 --> 00:01:10,117
Pressure is force divided by
area, so the pressure grows too.

26
00:01:10,517 --> 00:01:13,047
At a certain pressure, the weight lifts.

27
00:01:13,047 --> 00:01:15,066
Let's replay that in slow motion.

28
00:01:15,066 --> 00:01:17,039
Force up beats the weight down.

29
00:01:17,489 --> 00:01:20,778
The weight jumps, steam
escapes, and the pressure drops.

30
00:01:20,778 --> 00:01:22,114
Then it builds again.

31
00:01:22,614 --> 00:01:26,017
On the graph, pressure climbs,
drops, and climbs again.

32
00:01:26,017 --> 00:01:27,657
Every whistle is one peak.

33
00:01:28,307 --> 00:01:32,567
Now let's build the dimensional
formula of pressure, block by block.

34
00:01:32,917 --> 00:01:33,865
Step one.

35
00:01:33,865 --> 00:01:36,525
Velocity is displacement over time.

36
00:01:36,525 --> 00:01:38,444
LT to the minus one.

37
00:01:39,194 --> 00:01:40,149
Step two.

38
00:01:40,149 --> 00:01:42,826
Acceleration is velocity over time.

39
00:01:42,826 --> 00:01:44,758
LT to the minus two.

40
00:01:45,508 --> 00:01:46,542
Step three.

41
00:01:46,542 --> 00:01:49,013
Force is mass times acceleration.

42
00:01:49,013 --> 00:01:51,058
MLT to the minus two.

43
00:01:51,808 --> 00:01:52,758
Step four.

44
00:01:52,758 --> 00:01:54,887
Pressure is force over area.

45
00:01:54,887 --> 00:01:56,404
Area is L squared.

46
00:01:57,154 --> 00:02:02,726
MLT to the minus two, divided by L
squared, is ML to the minus one T

47
00:02:02,726 --> 00:02:04,238
to the minus two.

48
00:02:04,888 --> 00:02:07,229
Let's check each power, link by link.

49
00:02:07,579 --> 00:02:09,747
Mass came only from the force.

50
00:02:09,747 --> 00:02:10,918
One M on top.

51
00:02:10,918 --> 00:02:12,890
So the power of M is one.

52
00:02:13,290 --> 00:02:17,495
Length: one L on top from the
force, two below from the area.

53
00:02:17,495 --> 00:02:19,421
One minus two is minus one.

54
00:02:19,821 --> 00:02:23,983
Time came only from the
acceleration, divided by time twice.

55
00:02:23,983 --> 00:02:26,386
So the power of T is minus two.

56
00:02:26,986 --> 00:02:28,103
Remember this.

57
00:02:28,103 --> 00:02:32,936
To find a dimensional formula, start
from a known formula and replace each

58
00:02:32,936 --> 00:02:34,857
quantity by its dimensions.

59
00:02:35,607 --> 00:02:36,826
Side by side.

60
00:02:36,826 --> 00:02:39,525
Force is MLT to the minus two.

61
00:02:39,525 --> 00:02:41,331
It is the total push.

62
00:02:41,731 --> 00:02:45,394
Pressure is ML to the minus
one T to the minus two.

63
00:02:45,394 --> 00:02:47,523
The push on each square metre.

64
00:02:47,523 --> 00:02:49,552
Only the power of L changes.

65
00:02:50,152 --> 00:02:51,196
Now you try.

66
00:02:51,196 --> 00:02:54,450
A small pin and a big
plate get the same push.

67
00:02:54,450 --> 00:02:56,843
Which one gets the bigger pressure?

68
00:02:56,843 --> 00:02:58,140
Pause and decide.

69
00:03:01,340 --> 00:03:02,240
The pin!

70
00:03:02,118 --> 00:03:06,979
Area sits below the line, so a tiny
area means a big pressure for the same

71
00:03:06,979 --> 00:03:07,879
force.

72
00:03:08,245 --> 00:03:11,266
With the same blocks, we
can build energy and work.

73
00:03:11,616 --> 00:03:13,644
Work is force times distance.

74
00:03:13,644 --> 00:03:18,744
MLT to the minus two, times L,
gives ML squared T to the minus two.

75
00:03:19,144 --> 00:03:21,544
Kinetic energy is half m v squared.

76
00:03:21,544 --> 00:03:25,025
The half is a pure number,
so it has no dimension.

77
00:03:25,425 --> 00:03:26,356
Your turn.

78
00:03:26,356 --> 00:03:30,817
Does half m v squared have the
same dimensional formula as work?

79
00:03:30,817 --> 00:03:32,187
Pause and decide.

80
00:03:35,387 --> 00:03:36,287
Yes!

81
00:03:35,920 --> 00:03:41,334
M times LT to the minus one, squared,
is ML squared T to the minus two.

82
00:03:41,334 --> 00:03:43,655
That is why both use the joule.

83
00:03:44,305 --> 00:03:46,040
Now, one worked example.

84
00:03:46,390 --> 00:03:49,067
Find the dimensional formula of power.

85
00:03:49,067 --> 00:03:51,649
Power is work done divided by time.

86
00:03:52,149 --> 00:03:53,049
Step one.

87
00:03:53,024 --> 00:03:56,014
Work is ML squared T to the minus two.

88
00:03:56,764 --> 00:03:57,762
Step two.

89
00:03:57,762 --> 00:03:58,893
Time is T.

90
00:03:59,643 --> 00:04:00,578
Step three.

91
00:04:00,578 --> 00:04:01,478
Divide.

92
00:04:01,249 --> 00:04:05,505
T to the minus two, divided
by T, is T to the minus three.

93
00:04:06,255 --> 00:04:09,309
So power is ML squared
T to the minus three.

94
00:04:09,309 --> 00:04:12,392
Its unit, the watt, is
one joule per second.

95
00:04:13,042 --> 00:04:14,507
Now, the exam trap.

96
00:04:14,857 --> 00:04:19,669
Many students write force as MLT
squared, forgetting the minus sign.

97
00:04:20,019 --> 00:04:23,267
But time sits below the
line in acceleration.

98
00:04:23,267 --> 00:04:25,611
Dividing gives a negative power.

99
00:04:25,611 --> 00:04:28,216
Force is MLT to the minus two.

100
00:04:28,866 --> 00:04:30,295
Where is this asked?

101
00:04:30,295 --> 00:04:34,677
Short questions: write the formula
of a quantity, or match quantities to

102
00:04:34,677 --> 00:04:35,577
formulae.

103
00:04:36,006 --> 00:04:37,236
Exam level now.

104
00:04:37,236 --> 00:04:40,071
Surface tension is force per unit length.

105
00:04:40,071 --> 00:04:42,312
What is its dimensional formula?

106
00:04:42,312 --> 00:04:43,594
Pause and solve.

107
00:04:48,994 --> 00:04:50,420
The answer is B.

108
00:04:50,420 --> 00:04:52,256
MT to the minus two.

109
00:04:52,756 --> 00:04:55,457
Force is MLT to the minus two.

110
00:04:55,457 --> 00:04:58,136
Per unit length means divide by L.

111
00:04:58,636 --> 00:05:02,189
The L cancels, leaving
MT to the minus two.

112
00:05:02,189 --> 00:05:03,295
A is force.

113
00:05:03,295 --> 00:05:04,569
C is pressure.

114
00:05:04,569 --> 00:05:05,731
D is energy.

115
00:05:06,331 --> 00:05:07,788
Here is your recap.

116
00:05:07,788 --> 00:05:09,285
Screenshot this card.

117
00:05:12,485 --> 00:05:15,321
Can you answer these three
questions without help?

118
00:05:15,721 --> 00:05:16,621
One.

119
00:05:16,236 --> 00:05:21,384
What is the dimensional formula of force,
and why is the power of T negative?

120
00:05:22,284 --> 00:05:23,184
Two.

121
00:05:22,780 --> 00:05:25,592
Why does pressure have L to the minus one?

122
00:05:26,492 --> 00:05:27,392
Three.

123
00:05:27,125 --> 00:05:29,951
What is the dimensional formula of power?

124
00:05:31,051 --> 00:05:35,538
Next time: can dimensions prove a
friend's formula wrong in one line?

125
00:05:35,538 --> 00:05:39,141
We find out in the principle
of dimensional homogeneity.
